      "content": "It’s possible that the temperature or pressure settings might need adjustments. Try increasing the heat up to 295°F (145°C) and press the fabric at a higher pressure, around 4 to 6 pounds per square inch. Additionally, make sure the sublimation ink is not old, and the substrate material (foil) isn't aged or damaged. Also, ensure proper drying time before pressing. If the issue persists, consider checking the quality of your ink and substrates.",
